course: dictionary
lesson: 10561
title: Family words: uncle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An uncle is the brother of your mother or father. «Zara got a gift card and thanked her uncle anyway» tells you the uncle gave her a present, so he is a family member. Context clues help you work out who someone is.
explain: Uncle has two more meanings. An uncle is also the husband of your aunt, so if your aunt is married to a man, he is your uncle. Some children also call a close family friend «uncle», even when they are not related at all.
explain: Look at the words around uncle to see which meaning fits. «My uncle» with a name, like «Uncle Tom», means a relative or a family friend. The plural is uncles, and a great-uncle is your grandparent's brother.
fact: An uncle is the brother of your mother or father.
fact: An uncle is also the husband of your aunt.
fact: Some children call a close family friend «uncle».
fact: A great-uncle is your grandparent's brother.
fact: Cousins are the children of your aunts and uncles.
exercise: Zara's «uncle» gave her a gift card. Who is an uncle? | A teacher at school | *The brother of your mother or father | The mother of your cousin | A child in your class
exercise: A great-uncle is your grandparent's brother. Whose brother is a great-uncle? | *Your grandparent's | Your own brother's | Your best friend's
exercise: Ellie says «Uncle Sam» is coming to tea, but Sam is not related to her. What does uncle mean here? | A man who drives a bus | *A close family friend | A baby cousin | A family tree
test: What is the plural of uncle? | unclees | *uncles | uncled | uncle's
test: The husband of your aunt is your what? | brother | cousin | *uncle | grandparent
exam: Which sentence uses uncle to mean a close family friend? | *Some children call a close family friend «uncle» | Uncles are always older than their nieces | An uncle is a kind of tree | My cousin is an uncle
